":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":2978,"state":"closed","created_at":"2025-05-22T16:25:52Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T16:23:23Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-01-26T18:09:14Z"},"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-03-30T14:49:12Z","updated_at":"2026-01-08T21:04:26Z","closed_at":"2025-11-18T20:03:52Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104802","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104802","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104802.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104802.patch","merged_at":"2025-11-18T20:03:52Z"},"body":"- Fixes #104479\r\n\r\nThe problem was introduced in #99010 to fix an issue where the user was unable to resize the floating window or use buttons in the editor when the embedded game was activated on Windows. Prior to #99010, the window needed to be focused in order to be resized using the mouse. The modification, however, introduced a side effect: it reset the pressed keys in `Input` when hiding a window, because deactivation was no longer handled by the timer.\r\n\r\nBy retaining the timer solely for the deactivation process, the original issue remains resolved, and it also fixes #104479, as the pressed keys are no longer reset immediately when calling the `hide` method on a window.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptio